# .pii-allow — addresses guard-pii.mjs will not block.
#
# One entry per line. Either a literal address, or /a regex/ (case-insensitive).
# Blank lines and # comments ignored.
#
# EVERY LINE HERE IS A DECISION TO PUBLISH AN ADDRESS IN A PUBLIC REPOSITORY.
# That is the whole point of keeping the file: an exemption should appear in a
# diff, with a name attached, rather than being buried in the guard's source
# where nobody reviews it. Do not add a reader or member address here. If one
# needs to be in the repository, the answer is redaction, not an exemption.
#
# The broad structural exemptions (example.*, .invalid, .test, *.lan,
# @mereorthodoxy.com, users.noreply.github.com) live in scripts/guard-pii.mjs
# and are documented there, including the deliberate gap around staff
# addresses.

# Seeded 2026-08-20. Third-party and fixture addresses already in the tree at
# the time the guard was written, each verified as not belonging to a reader:

# Stripe's own checkout host, appears in payment-link copy.
/@checkout\.stripe\.com$/

# Ian's own address, in the package.json "author" field since the repo began.
iharber93@gmail.com
